course: dictionary
lesson: 1071
title: Words about class
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words describe groups of people in society, and bourgeois is one of them. Its first meaning describes the middle class: people who have comfortable jobs, homes and money.
explain: Look at the clues in «Louise Bourgeois made giant spider sculptures called Maman, French for mummy». The capital letter and the name Louise tell you Bourgeois is a person's surname, not the class word. Context shows you which meaning is being used.
explain: The sentence continues: «she said the spider stood for her mother, who repaired tapestries, patient and protective.» A tapestry is a woven picture, so repairing one takes care. The clues show that the mother was patient and caring.
explain: Bourgeois can also be an unkind word. When an adult says something is «a bit bourgeois, isn't it?», they mean it is too fussy and posh about being respectable. Check the tone: is the speaker praising it, or teasing?
fact: Bourgeois is an adjective (bourgeois) and a noun (a bourgeois, the bourgeoisie).
fact: «Bourgeois» means belonging to the middle class: people with comfortable jobs, homes and money.
fact: In history, especially in Karl Marx's ideas, the bourgeoisie are the people who own factories and businesses.
fact: Informally, and often unkindly, «bourgeois» means too interested in owning things, being respectable and following ordinary middle-class tastes.
fact: A capital B can mean a name, as in Louise Bourgeois the artist, so check the context.
exercise: Louise Bourgeois made giant spider sculptures called «Maman». What is Bourgeois in that sentence? | *A person's name | A type of tapestry | A factory owner | A kind of spider
exercise: In history, the bourgeoisie are the people who own what? | Forests and rivers | *Factories and businesses | Schools and hospitals | Castles and palaces
exercise: Someone says, «That café is a bit bourgeois, isn't it?» What do they probably mean? | It is very cheap and badly made | *It is too fussy and posh about respectability, said unkindly | It is a place full of spiders | It is loud and noisy
test: «She said the spider stood for her mother, who repaired tapestries, patient and protective.» What does patient mean here? | Angry about the spider | Tired of working | In a hurry | *Calm and willing to wait
test: What does bourgeois mean in its first meaning? | *Belonging to the middle class, with comfortable jobs, homes and money | Being very poor and hungry | Living in the countryside on a farm | Belonging to the royal family
exam: Which sentence uses bourgeois as a person's name? | «He was far too bourgeois for a camping trip.» | «The bourgeois family owned a comfortable home.» | «The bourgeoisie owned all the factories.» | *«Louise Bourgeois made giant spider sculptures.»
